[
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# The list as it stands, and the file's job is to keep proving that all of it arrives", "line": 1, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# at once rather than one invocation at a time.", "line": 2, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 3, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Rewritten ten times, and each rewrite is the gate working — `str` and `f64` at M5b,", "line": 4, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# `record` at M5c step 3, `array` at step 5, writing one element at step 6, `T?` and", "line": 5, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# `{K: V}` at M5d, and at M6 step 3 the three built-ins that used to stand here", "line": 6, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# (`sort`, `join`, `chars`) all acquired entry points. **Every type in the language", "line": 7, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# emits, and every Tier-1 built-in emits**, so what is left is three different KINDS of", "line": 8, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# refusal rather than three names:", "line": 9, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 10, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#   1. **the built-in row is GONE, and this paragraph is its headstone** (panel 084).", "line": 11, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      It was the gate's last row keyed on a value rather than a capability:", "line": 12, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      `sort` inside `sorted_first<A>(items: [A])`, instantiated at a record. The", "line": 13, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      reasoning was that the checker could not see it. Measured false —", "line": 14, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      `types/apply.rs:139` records every instantiation inside `types::check`, and", "line": 15, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      `sort` was the *single outlier* among restricted built-ins, since `join`,", "line": 16, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      `to_str`, `chars`, `keys`, `len`, `slice` and `repeat` all refuse `[A]` at", "line": 17, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      `heroes check` already. So it is `unordered_element` at exit 1 now, on the", "line": 18, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      author's line, and this file no longer carries the shape. The \"refused by", "line": 19, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      NAME\" row cannot fire either: all 23 reserved names have an entry point, a", "line": 20, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      library body or a lowering, and `emit/tests/gate.rs` asserts that partition", "line": 21, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      instead of an example;", "line": 22, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#   2. a GENERIC function and the six higher-order built-ins, which all emit now —", "line": 23, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      they are in the file to prove the two refusals are not about them;", "line": 24, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#   3. a UNIT-typed container element, which has no C declaration at all — `void t0;`", "line": 25, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      is a hard error, so the type that occupies no storage is refused where a", "line": 26, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      storage location is required.", "line": 27, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      Three rows have stopped being refusable rather than been implemented around:", "line": 28, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      function values at M6 step 5 (a plain C function pointer), generics at step 6", "line": 29, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      (one copy per type tuple, no template left), and `extern` at M-ffi-ladder step 5 —", "line": 30, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      the one whose reason was a veto rather than a milestone, and what lifted it", "line": 31, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#      was the `#include` arriving, exactly as §4.19 said it would.", "line": 32, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "#", "line": 33, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Everything else stays in the file deliberately: the record, the array, the element", "line": 34, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# write, the map, the `T?` and the six built-ins that now emit all work, so their", "line": 35, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# presence proves the refusals below are about those three capabilities and nothing", "line": 36, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# else.", "line": 37, "col": 1},
  {"kind": "comment", "text": "# Bulk regression case.", "line": 38, "col": 1},
